{
  "name": "guard_held_stumble",
  "note": "(anim-guard) The guard held from behind and pulled backwards (BRIEF \"Holding a guard\"): weight behind the heels (pelvis 7 cm behind the feet's mean, the chest arched back onto the holder ~15 deg, the chin tucked a little against the arm), knees soft all through, short catching steps backwards (0.3 m a step, 0.6 m a cycle: about 1.0 s a cycle at the hold's 0.6 m/s): the landing foot reaches back onto its ball, rolls flat and carries the weight forward under the body until it is the front foot, weight on its heel (toes up); then it is dragged back on its heel, skims 1.5-2 cm off the floor and reaches back again. The hands stay gripping the holder's forearm at the throat (guard_held_hands layers its struggle over this). Phase 0 is the left foot's landing behind; keys 0-0.375 are mirrored onto 0.5-0.875. Angles in degrees in the body frame (x right, y up, z forward): pitch about x (+ the top forward), yaw about y (+ turns right), roll about z (+ the right side up); pelvis offsets in cm from rest (Wren 1.68 m). Arms: flex (+ forward, chest frame), abd (+ out), elbow (+ bent), inward (the forearm turned in), wrist { yaw (twist about the forearm), pitch, roll } local to the forearm (anim-rig, RIG.md). Legs (preview and floor checks; the game feet come from the foot planner until a leg channel exists): flex (+ the knee forward), add (+ the foot in), knee (+ bent), ankle (+ the toes up). Keyed by hand from how a real person moves (no game reference); the feet were placed on the floor and the hands on the holder's forearm with a two-bone IK while authoring, then written here as plain angles: edit these numbers directly.",
